        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r145381405-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "A glimpse of culture and religion",
        "text": "This Hindu temple in Kathmandu gave me an amazing glimpse into another culture and religion. Situated on two banks of the river, it is, like many religious homes, also a site for funerals (and in this case, cremations). While we were there, several were going on. Our guide explained the rituals, then left us to observe or not, as we chose. While I realize this may not be for all, I found it interesting and enriching. One of the big reasons I travel is to experience and appreciate the cultures of others who are different than myself. I felt privileged to have visited here.\nNon-Hindu visitors may not visit the main temple on one side of the river, but may visit the opposite side, which in addition to providing a view of the main temple, also has various religious artifacts.",
