        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r145129969-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Worth the visit, but not for everybody's eyes",
        "text": "The place is one of the holliest hindu places. Here is where they bring their beloved ones to be cremated when they die. The architechture and perspectives are unique. Before going there you have to be aware that thi is a cremation place. You see dead people about to get cremated or in the process, so the smell is strong and in my case I could see human remains burning, which is not unexpected to see. If you are too sensitive, then you may avoid this place. Also be carefull if you are travelling with children. I personally do not recommend it, since there are too many monkeys and it's easy to fall in many places. Remember, this is a holy place in Nepal. It might be a different world and you will see many things you won't understand, so keep in mind that you are the visitor, this belongs to the hindus and it's up to them to understand and judge, not to us. Enjoy the experience and embrace the differences.",
